.TH INPUTWEAVE 1 "2026-10-29" "InputWeave" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inputweave \- share one keyboard and mouse across computers on a LAN
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inputweave agent
.br
.B inputweave ctl
.RI [ options ] " command"
.br
.B inputweave identity
.SH DESCRIPTION
InputWeave lets the computers on a desk share one keyboard and mouse: the
pointer moves off the edge of one screen onto the computer next to it. It
also carries the clipboard and sends files between them.
.PP
.B inputweave agent
is the background service. It runs as each user's systemd service,
.BR app-cc.ctsite.inputweave@agent.service ,
which starts with the desktop session. On Wayland it asks the desktop for
remote control and input capture through its portals; the InputWeave app
(\fBinputweave-app\fR(1)) asks for them the first time.
.PP
.B inputweave ctl
talks to the running agent: \fBstatus\fR, \fBnearby\fR, \fBpair\fR,
\fBsend\fR, \fBtransfers\fR, \fBlayout\fR, \fBhotkeys\fR, \fBdiagnose\fR and
more; \fBinputweave ctl --help\fR lists them all.
.PP
.B inputweave identity
prints this computer's certificate fingerprint, for listing it in another
computer's configuration file without pairing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/inputweave/config.toml
The configuration file, read when the agent starts.
.TP
.I ~/.config/inputweave/devices.toml
Paired devices, their arrangement and the settings changed in the app.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/inputweave/agent.sock
The agent's socket for the app and \fBinputweave ctl\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR inputweave-app (1),
.BR journalctl (1):
\fBjournalctl \-\-user \-u app-cc.ctsite.inputweave@agent.service\fR shows
the agent's log.
